      "response": "Warning: Unknown toolsets: agency-runtime, async-delegation, messaging\n```python\ndef average(values):\n    if not values:\n        raise ValueError(\"average() requires at least one value\")\n    return sum(values) / len(values)\n```\n\nDefects in the supplied function:\n- Uses `//`, so it floors instead of returning the arithmetic mean with fractional results.\n- Negative fractional means are especially wrong because `//` floors toward negative infinity.\n- Empty input raises `ZeroDivisionError`; the requested behavior is `ValueError`.\n\nFocused regression tests:\n\n```python\nimport pytest\n\n\ndef test_average_float_values_returns_fractional_mean():\n    assert average([1.0, 2.0]) == 1.5\n\n\ndef test_average_negative_numbers_returns_fractional_mean():\n    assert average([-1, -2]) == -1.5\n\n\ndef test_average_empty_input_raises_value_error():\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        average([])\n```\n\nSkipped file reads/edits and test execution per your boundary.\n",
